  "2018 P1 Q12": {"skill":"A vector in components, then a parameter from its magnitude.","method":"(a) 1 mark, (b) 3 marks","moves":["(a) Double each component of \\(\\mathbf{a}\\), then add \\(\\mathbf{b}\\).","(b) Write the magnitude of \\(2\\mathbf{a} + \\mathbf{b}\\) using its components.","(b) Set it equal to \\(7\\), square both sides, and solve for \\(p\\)."],"marks":[1,1,2],"shows":["\\(\\begin{pmatrix}6\\\\-3\\\\4 + p\\end{pmatrix}\\)","\\(\\sqrt{6^2 + (-3)^2 + (4 + p)^2}\\)","\\(45 + (4 + p)^2 = 49 \\Rightarrow (4 + p)^2 = 4\\) or \\(p^2 + 8p + 12 = 0\\)"]},
  "2018 P1 Q13": {"skill":"Double angle values, then \\(\\sin 3x\\) as \\(\\sin(2x + x)\\).","method":"4 marks, (b) 3 marks","moves":["(a)(i) Use Pythagoras on the triangle to find the third side, then write \\(\\cos x\\).","(a)(i) Use \\(\\sin 2x = 2\\sin x\\cos x\\) and simplify.","(a)(ii) Use a formula for \\(\\cos 2x\\), eg \\(1 - 2\\sin^2 x\\).","(b) Expand \\(\\sin(2x + x)\\) with the addition formula.","(b) Substitute your values, and simplify."],"marks":[1,2,1,1,2],"shows":["\\(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{11}}\\)","\\(2 \\times \\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{11}} \\times \\dfrac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{11}}\\)","\\(\\dfrac{3}{11}\\)","\\(\\sin 2x\\cos x + \\cos 2x\\sin x\\)","\\(\\dfrac{4\\sqrt{7}}{11} \\times \\dfrac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{11}} + \\dfrac{3}{11} \\times \\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{11}}\\)"]},
  "2018 P1 Q14": {"skill":"A definite integral of a bracket to a negative fractional power.","method":"5 marks","moves":["Write the integrand as a power: \\((2x + 9)^{-\\frac{2}{3}}\\).","Raise the power by \\(1\\) and divide by the new power, then divide by \\(2\\), the coefficient of \\(x\\).","Substitute the limits and evaluate (the cube roots are exact)."],"marks":[1,2,2],"shows":["\\((2x + 9)^{-\\frac{2}{3}}\\)","\\(\\dfrac{(2x + 9)^{\\frac{1}{3}}}{\\frac{1}{3}} \\ldots\\)","\\(\\dfrac{3}{2}(2(9) + 9)^{\\frac{1}{3}} - \\dfrac{3}{2}(2(-4) + 9)^{\\frac{1}{3}}\\)"]},
  "2018 P1 Q15": {"skill":"Sketching a cubic from its roots and stationary points.","method":"4 marks","moves":["Mark the root at \\(x = -4\\) and the repeated root at \\(x = 2\\), where the curve touches the axis.","There is also a stationary point at \\(x = -2\\).","\\(f'(0) > 0\\) means the curve is rising where it crosses the \\(y\\)-axis: use that to decide the orientation, and sketch."],"marks":[2,1,1],"shows":["sketch of a negative cubic: falling from the top left through \\(x = -4\\) to a minimum at \\(x = -2\\), rising to touch the \\(x\\)-axis at \\(x = 2\\), then falling","(as )",null]},
  "2018 P1 Q2": {"skill":"The inverse of a linear function.","method":"3 marks","moves":["Write \\(y = \\frac{1}{5}x - 4\\) and add \\(4\\) to both sides.","Multiply by \\(5\\) to get \\(x\\) in terms of \\(y\\).","Swap the letters back to write \\(g^{-1}(x)\\)."],"marks":[1,1,1],"shows":["\\(g(g^{-1}(x)) = x\\)","\\(\\dfrac{1}{5}g^{-1}(x) - 4 = x\\)",null]},
