  "2018 P1 Q9": {"skill":"Vector pathways in a triangular prism.","method":"(a) 1 mark, (b) 2 marks","moves":["(a) Go from \\(B\\) back to \\(A\\), then along to \\(C\\).","(b) Choose a route from \\(M\\) to \\(D\\), eg \\(M\\) to \\(C\\) (half of \\(BC\\)), then \\(C\\) to \\(A\\), then \\(A\\) to \\(D\\).","(b) Write each part in \\(\\mathbf{t}\\), \\(\\mathbf{u}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{v}\\) and simplify."],"marks":[1,1,1],"shows":["\\(-\\mathbf{t} + \\mathbf{u}\\)","\\(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\overrightarrow{BC} + \\overrightarrow{CA} + \\overrightarrow{AD}\\)",null]},
  "2018 P2 Q1": {"skill":"The area under a parabola between its roots.","method":"4 marks","moves":["Find where the curve crosses the \\(x\\)-axis to get the limits, and write the integral.","Integrate each term.","Substitute the limits and evaluate."],"marks":[1,1,2],"shows":["\\(\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^{3}(3 + 2x - x^2)\\,dx\\)","\\(3x + \\dfrac{2x^2}{2} - \\dfrac{x^3}{3}\\)","\\(\\left(3 \\times 3 + \\dfrac{2 \\times 3^2}{2} - \\dfrac{3^3}{3}\\right) - \\left(3 \\times (-1) + \\dfrac{2 \\times (-1)^2}{2} - \\dfrac{(-1)^3}{3}\\right)\\)"]},
  "2018 P2 Q10": {"skill":"The discriminant: two real and distinct roots.","method":"4 marks","moves":["Write the discriminant \\(b^2 - 4ac\\) with \\(a = 1\\), \\(b = m - 3\\) and \\(c = m\\).","Expand and find where it is \\(0\\).","Two real and distinct roots means the discriminant is greater than \\(0\\): use a sketch to state the range."],"marks":[1,1,2],"shows":["\\((m - 3)^2 - 4 \\times 1 \\times m\\)","\\(1, 9\\)","\\((m - 3)^2 - 4 \\times 1 \\times m > 0\\)"]},
  "2018 P2 Q11": {"skill":"An exponential model: finding \\(k\\), then a percentage.","method":"(a) 4 marks, (b) 2 marks","moves":["(a) Substitute \\(P = 50\\) and \\(t = 3\\), and get \\(e^{3k}\\) on its own.","(a) Take natural logs of both sides and solve for \\(k\\).","(b) Substitute \\(t = 5\\) to find the percentage who wait less than \\(5\\) minutes, then take it from \\(100\\)."],"marks":[2,2,2],"shows":["\\(50 = 100(1 - e^{3k})\\)","\\(\\ln 0.5 = 3k\\)","\\(68.5\\)"]},
  "2018 P2 Q12": {"skill":"Two circles: a centre, a constant, a dividing ratio, and a third circle.","method":"6 marks, (c) 1 mark","moves":["(a) Read the centre of \\(C_1\\) from its equation, then substitute it into \\(C_2\\)'s equation to find \\(c\\).","(b)(i) Find both radii and the distance between the centres, and use them to write the ratio.","(b)(ii) Find the centre of \\(C_2\\), then use the ratio to find \\(P\\).","(c) \\(C_2\\) is inside \\(C_3\\) and touches it: the radius of \\(C_3\\) is the distance from \\(P\\) to \\(C_2\\)'s centre plus \\(C_2\\)'s radius."],"marks":[2,2,2,1],"shows":[null,"two from \\(r_2 = 25\\), \\(r_1 = 10\\) and \\(r_2 - r_1 = 15\\)","\\((-7, 11)\\) or \\(\\begin{pmatrix}-7\\\\11\\end{pmatrix}\\)",null]},
  "2018 P2 Q2": {"skill":"The scalar product, then the angle between two vectors.","method":"(a) 1 mark, (b) 4 marks","moves":["(a) Multiply matching components and add.","(b) Find the magnitude of each vector.","(b) Use \\(\\cos\\theta = \\frac{\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{v}}{|\\mathbf{u}||\\mathbf{v}|}\\), then take the inverse cos."],"marks":[1,2,2],"shows":[null,"\\(\\sqrt{26}\\)","\\(\\cos\\theta^\\circ = \\dfrac{24}{\\sqrt{26}\\sqrt{138}}\\)"]},
  "2018 P2 Q3": {"skill":"Increasing or decreasing at a point.","method":"3 marks","moves":["Differentiate \\(f(x)\\).","Substitute \\(x = 2\\) into the derivative.","A positive derivative means increasing, a negative one decreasing: say which."],"marks":[1,1,1],"shows":["\\(3x^2 - 7\\)","\\(5\\)",null]},
