  "2018 P2 Q5": {"skill":"A perpendicular bisector, the circumcentre, and the circumcircle.","method":"(a) 3 marks, (b) 2 marks, (c) 2 marks","moves":["(a) Find the midpoint of \\(PQ\\).","(a) Find the gradient of \\(PQ\\) and the perpendicular gradient, and write \\(L_1\\) through the midpoint.","(b) Solve \\(L_1\\) and \\(L_2\\) simultaneously.","(c) The radius is the distance from \\(C\\) to \\(P\\) (or \\(Q\\)): find it and write the equation."],"marks":[1,2,2,2],"shows":["\\((6, 1)\\)","\\(-1 \\Rightarrow m_{\\text{perp}} = 1\\)",null,"\\(\\sqrt{50}\\)"]},
  "2018 P2 Q6": {"skill":"Composite trig functions, then solving where they are equal.","method":"3 marks, (b) 6 marks","moves":["(a) \\(f(g(x))\\) means put \\(g(x) = 2x\\) into \\(f\\) wherever there is an \\(x\\).","(a) \\(g(f(x))\\) means double \\(f(x)\\).","(b) Set the two equal, and replace \\(\\cos 2x\\) with \\(2\\cos^2 x - 1\\).","(b) Rearrange into a quadratic in \\(\\cos x\\) equal to \\(0\\), and factorise.","(b) Solve each factor for \\(\\cos x\\), then find \\(x\\) in \\(0 \\le x < 2\\pi\\) (one factor has no solutions)."],"marks":[2,1,2,2,2],"shows":["\\(f(2x)\\)","\\(2(3 + \\cos x)\\)","\\(3 + \\cos 2x = 2(3 + \\cos x)\\)","\\(2\\cos^2 x - 2\\cos x - 4 = 0\\)","\\(\\cos x = 2\\), \\(\\cos x = -1\\)"]},
  "2018 P2 Q7": {"skill":"Factorising a cubic, then the recurrence relation it comes from.","method":"8 marks, (b) 1 mark","moves":["(a) Use synthetic division with \\(2\\), get a remainder of \\(0\\), and say what that shows.","(a) Write down the quadratic factor from the bottom row, and factorise fully.","(b) Apply the recurrence relation twice from \\(u_5\\), expanding each time.","(c)(i) Set \\(u_7 = u_5\\) and arrange it as a cubic in \\(a\\) equal to \\(0\\).","(c)(i) It is the cubic in (a), with \\(a\\) in place of \\(x\\): use its roots, and keep the one that lets a limit exist.","(c)(ii) At the limit, \\(L = aL - 1\\). Solve for \\(L\\)."],"marks":[2,2,1,1,2,1],"shows":["synthetic division by \\(2\\) on \\(2\\ \\ {-3}\\ \\ {-3}\\ \\ 2\\), or \\(2 \\times (2)^3 - 3(2)^2 - 3 \\times (2) + 2\\)","\\(2x^2 + x - 1\\)","\\(u_6 = a(2a - 3) - 1 = 2a^2 - 3a - 1\\) leading to \\(u_7 = a(2a^2 - 3a - 1) - 1 = 2a^3 - 3a^2 - a - 1\\)","\\(2a^3 - 3a^2 - 3a + 2 = 0\\)",null,null]},
  "2018 P2 Q8": {"skill":"The wave function as \\(k\\cos(x - a)\\), then a minimum and where it occurs.","method":"(a) 4 marks, 3 marks","moves":["(a) Expand \\(k\\cos(x - a)\\) and compare coefficients with \\(2\\cos x - \\sin x\\).","(a) Find \\(k\\), then find \\(a\\) from \\(\\tan a\\), checking which quadrant it is in.","(b)(i) \\(6\\cos x - 3\\sin x\\) is \\(3\\) times the expression in (a), so its minimum is \\(-3k\\).","(b)(ii) The minimum is where \\(x - a = 180\\). Solve and keep the answer in \\(0 \\le x < 360\\)."],"marks":[2,2,1,2],"shows":["\\(k\\cos x^\\circ\\cos a^\\circ + k\\sin x^\\circ\\sin a^\\circ\\) stated explicitly",null,"\\(-3\\sqrt{5}\\) or \\(-\\sqrt{45}\\)","\\(x - 333.4 = 180\\) leading to \\(x = 513.4\\)"]},
  "2018 P2 Q9": {"skill":"The minimum perimeter of a sector.","method":"6 marks","moves":["Write \\(P\\) with a negative power: \\(2x + 128x^{-1}\\).","Differentiate and set the derivative equal to \\(0\\).","Solve for \\(x\\).","Show it is a minimum, and substitute to find \\(P\\)."],"marks":[1,2,1,2],"shows":["\\(2x + 128x^{-1}\\)","\\(2 - \\dfrac{128}{x^2}\\)","\\(8\\)","table of signs for a derivative \\(\\therefore\\) minimum; or \\(P''(8) = \\dfrac{1}{2} > 0 \\therefore\\) minimum"]},
