  "2019 P1 Q5": {"skill":"Collinear points in 3D, then the ratio.","method":"(a) 3 marks, (b) 1 mark","moves":["(a) Find the vectors \\(\\overrightarrow{AB}\\) and \\(\\overrightarrow{BC}\\).","(a) Show one is a multiple of the other.","(a) Say they are parallel, share the point \\(B\\), and so \\(A\\), \\(B\\) and \\(C\\) are collinear.","(b) Use that multiple to write the ratio \\(AB : BC\\)."],"marks":[1,1,1,1],"shows":["\\(\\overrightarrow{AB} = \\begin{pmatrix}3\\\\-6\\\\3\\end{pmatrix}\\)","\\(\\overrightarrow{BC} = \\begin{pmatrix}4\\\\-8\\\\4\\end{pmatrix} \\therefore \\overrightarrow{AB} = \\dfrac{3}{4}\\overrightarrow{BC}\\)","\\(\\ldots \\Rightarrow\\) AB is parallel to BC (common direction) and B is a common point \\(\\Rightarrow\\) A, B and C are collinear",null]},
