  "2019 P1 Q8": {"skill":"The area between two parabolas.","method":"(a) 1 mark, (b) 3 marks","moves":["(a) Write the integral of upper curve minus lower curve, from \\(x = -1\\) to \\(x = 2\\), and simplify the integrand.","(b) Integrate each term.","(b) Substitute the limits and evaluate."],"marks":[1,1,2],"shows":["\\(\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^{2}(-x^2 + x + 2)\\,dx\\)","\\(-\\dfrac{1}{3}x^3 + \\dfrac{1}{2}x^2 + 2x\\)","\\(\\left(-\\dfrac{1}{3}(2)^3 + \\dfrac{1}{2}(2)^2 + 2(2)\\right) - \\left(-\\dfrac{1}{3}(-1)^3 + \\dfrac{1}{2}(-1)^2 + 2(-1)\\right)\\)"]},
  "2019 P1 Q9": {"skill":"The scalar product with a parameter: perpendicular, then parallel.","method":"4 marks, (b) 2 marks","moves":["(a)(i) Multiply matching components and add.","(a)(ii) Perpendicular means the scalar product is \\(0\\): set it equal to \\(0\\).","(a)(ii) Factorise and solve for \\(p\\).","(b) Parallel means one vector is a multiple of the other: use the second and third components to find the multiple, then solve for \\(p\\)."],"marks":[1,1,2,2],"shows":["\\(p(2p + 16) + (-2)(-3) + (4)(6)\\)","\\(p(2p + 16) + (-2)(-3) + (4)(6) = 0\\)","\\(2(p + 5)(p + 3)\\)","\\(3(p) = 2(2p + 16)\\) or \\(3\\mathbf{u} = 2\\mathbf{v}\\)"]},
  "2019 P2 Q1": {"skill":"A median, an altitude, and where they meet.","method":"(a) 3 marks, (b) 3 marks, (c) 2 marks","moves":["(a) \\(D\\) is the midpoint of \\(AC\\): find it.","(a) Find the gradient of \\(BD\\), and write the equation.","(b) The altitude \\(AE\\) is perpendicular to \\(BC\\): find the gradient of \\(BC\\), then the perpendicular gradient.","(b) Use that gradient and point \\(A\\) in \\(y - b = m(x - a)\\).","(c) Solve the two equations simultaneously."],"marks":[1,2,2,1,2],"shows":["\\((-4, -3)\\)","\\(-\\dfrac{1}{3}\\)",null,null,"\\(x = 2\\) or \\(y = -5\\)"]},
  "2019 P2 Q10": {"skill":"The factor theorem, then factorising a quartic with an irreducible quadratic.","method":"(a) 2 marks, (b) 5 marks","moves":["(a) Use synthetic division with \\(-3\\), get a remainder of \\(0\\), and say what that shows.","(b) Take the cubic from the bottom row of (a) and try another value until the remainder is \\(0\\).","(b) Write down the quadratic left over, and work out its discriminant.","(b) Say what the discriminant tells you, and write the full factorisation."],"marks":[2,2,2,1],"shows":["synthetic division by \\(-3\\) on \\(3\\ \\ 10\\ \\ 1\\ \\ {-8}\\ \\ {-6}\\), or \\(3 \\times (-3)^4 + 10 \\times (-3)^3 + (-3)^2 - 8 \\times (-3) - 6\\)","synthetic division of \\(3\\ \\ 1\\ \\ {-2}\\ \\ {-2}\\)",null,null]},
  "2019 P2 Q11": {"skill":"The surface area of a box with a tunnel, then its minimum.","method":"(a) 3 marks, (b) 6 marks","moves":["(a) Add the areas of every surface, including the four inside the tunnel.","(a) Use the volume, \\(2000\\), to write \\(h\\) in terms of \\(x\\), then substitute.","(b) Write \\(A\\) with a negative power of \\(x\\), ready to differentiate.","(b) Differentiate and set the derivative equal to \\(0\\).","(b) Solve for \\(x\\).","(b) Show it is a minimum, and substitute to find \\(A\\)."],"marks":[1,2,1,2,1,2],"shows":["\\(\\ 16x^2 + 16xh\\)","\\(h = \\dfrac{2000}{8x^2}\\)","\\(16x^2 + 4000x^{-1}\\)","\\(32x - 4000x^{-2}\\)","\\(5\\)","table of signs for a derivative \\(\\therefore\\) minimum; or \\(A''(x) = 96 > 0 \\Rightarrow\\) minimum"]},
  "2019 P2 Q12": {"skill":"From a straight-line graph of \\(\\log_4 y\\) against \\(x\\) to \\(y = ab^x\\).","method":"5 marks","moves":["Read the gradient and the intercept off the graph, and write the line as \\(\\log_4 y = mx + c\\).","Write it in exponential form: \\(y = 4^{mx + c}\\).","Split the power with the laws of indices.","Compare with \\(y = ab^x\\) to state \\(a\\) and \\(b\\)."],"marks":[1,1,1,2],"shows":["\\(\\log_4 y = 3x - 1\\)","\\(\\log_4 y = 3x\\log_4 4 - \\log_4 4\\)","\\(\\log_4 y = \\log_4 4^{3x} - \\log_4 4\\)","\\(\\log_4 y = \\log_4\\left(\\dfrac{4^{3x}}{4}\\right)\\) or \\(\\log_4 y = \\log_4 4^{-1}4^{3x}\\)"]},
  "2019 P2 Q13": {"skill":"Finding \\(f(x)\\) from its rate of change and a root.","method":"5 marks","moves":["\\(f(x)\\) is the integral of its rate of change: write down what you need to integrate.","Integrate each term and add \\(+ c\\).","The graph crosses the \\(x\\)-axis at \\((7, 0)\\): substitute to find \\(c\\), and write \\(f(x)\\)."],"marks":[1,2,2],"shows":["\\(f'(x) = 3x^2 - 16x + 11\\) or \\(f(x) = \\displaystyle\\int(3x^2 - 16x + 11)\\,dx\\)","\\(\\dfrac{3x^3}{3} - \\dfrac{16x^2}{2} \\ldots\\)","\\(0 = 7^3 - 8 \\times 7^2 + 11 \\times 7 + c\\)"]},
  "2019 P2 Q14": {"skill":"The angle between vectors from \\(\\mathbf{u} \\cdot (\\mathbf{u} + \\mathbf{v})\\).","method":"4 marks","moves":["Expand \\(\\mathbf{u} \\cdot (\\mathbf{u} + \\mathbf{v})\\) into \\(\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{u} + \\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{v}\\).","\\(\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{u}\\) is \\(|\\mathbf{u}|^2\\): evaluate it, and find \\(\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{v}\\).","Use \\(\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{v} = |\\mathbf{u}||\\mathbf{v}|\\cos\\theta\\) to find \\(\\cos\\theta\\), then the angle."],"marks":[1,1,2],"shows":["\\(\\mathbf{u}.\\mathbf{u} + \\mathbf{u}.\\mathbf{v}\\)","\\(16\\)","\\(20\\cos\\theta = 5\\) or \\(\\cos\\theta = \\dfrac{5}{20}\\)"]},
  "2019 P2 Q15": {"skill":"A tangent to a circle, then the circle through C, P and T.","method":"(a) 3 marks, 4 marks","moves":["(a) Find the gradient of the radius \\(CP\\), then the perpendicular gradient.","(a) Write the equation of the tangent through \\(P\\).","(b)(i) Put \\(x = 0\\) into the tangent.","(b)(ii) The angle at \\(P\\) is a right angle, so \\(CT\\) is a diameter: find its midpoint.","(b)(ii) Find the radius, and write the equation of the circle."],"marks":[2,1,1,1,2],"shows":["\\(-\\dfrac{1}{3}\\)",null,null,"\\((4, 5)\\)","\\(\\sqrt{65}\\)"]},
  "2019 P2 Q2": {"skill":"Integrating a root, a negative power and a constant.","method":"4 marks","moves":["Write \\(6\\sqrt{x}\\) as a power: \\(6x^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\).","Integrate each term: raise the power by \\(1\\) and divide by the new power.","Simplify the coefficients and add \\(+ c\\)."],"marks":[1,2,1],"shows":["\\(6x^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\)","\\(\\dfrac{6x^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{\\frac{3}{2}} \\ldots\\)",null]},
  "2019 P2 Q3": {"skill":"Vector pathways in a pyramid.","method":"(a) 1 mark, (b) 2 marks","moves":["(a) Go from \\(B\\) back to \\(A\\), then up to \\(E\\).","(b) Choose a route from \\(E\\) to \\(F\\), eg \\(E\\) to \\(B\\) then \\(B\\) to \\(F\\).","(b) \\(\\overrightarrow{BF}\\) is \\(\\frac{3}{4}\\) of \\(\\overrightarrow{BC}\\), and \\(\\overrightarrow{BC}\\) is the same as \\(\\overrightarrow{AD}\\): write the route in \\(\\mathbf{p}\\), \\(\\mathbf{q}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{r}\\)."],"marks":[1,1,1],"shows":[null,"\\(\\overrightarrow{EB} + \\overrightarrow{BF}\\)",null]},
  "2019 P2 Q4": {"skill":"A recurrence relation model: form it, justify a limit, find it.","method":"(a) 1 mark, 3 marks","moves":["(a) Falling by \\(2.7\\%\\) leaves \\(97.3\\%\\) each year, and \\(30\\) are added: state \\(a\\) and \\(b\\).","(b)(i) A limit exists when the multiplier is strictly between \\(-1\\) and \\(1\\): say what it is and that it is.","(b)(ii) At the limit, \\(L = aL + b\\). Solve for \\(L\\) and round to the nearest hundred."],"marks":[1,1,2],"shows":[null,"a limit exists as the recurrence relation is linear and \\(-1 < 0.973 < 1\\)","\\(L = 0.973L + 30\\) or \\(L = \\dfrac{30}{1 - 0.973}\\)"]},
  "2019 P2 Q5": {"skill":"Sketching the derived function of a cubic.","method":"2 marks","moves":["\\(g'(x)\\) is \\(0\\) at the stationary points of \\(g\\), so its graph crosses the \\(x\\)-axis at \\(x = -2\\) and \\(x = 4\\).","Decide where \\(g\\) is increasing (\\(g'\\) positive) and decreasing (\\(g'\\) negative), and sketch the parabola."],"marks":[1,1],"shows":["parabola with roots at \\(-2\\) and \\(4\\)",null]},
