  "2022 P2 Q4": {"skill":"Area above the axis, then the total area with a part below.","method":"(a) 4 marks, (b) 3 marks","moves":["(a) Set up the integral of the curve between the roots either side of the area above the axis.","(a) Integrate each term.","(a) Substitute the limits and evaluate.","(b) Integrate between the other two roots. The answer is negative because that area is below the axis.","(b) Add the size of that area to your answer to (a)."],"marks":[1,1,2,2,1],"shows":["\\(\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^{2}(x^3 - 5x^2 + 2x + 8)\\,dx\\)","\\(\\dfrac{1}{4}x^4 - \\dfrac{5}{3}x^3 + \\dfrac{2x^2}{2} + 8x\\)","\\(\\left(\\dfrac{1}{4}(2)^4 - \\dfrac{5}{3}(2)^3 + (2)^2 + 8(2)\\right) - \\left(\\dfrac{1}{4}(-1)^4 - \\dfrac{5}{3}(-1)^3 + (-1)^2 + 8(-1)\\right)\\)","\\(\\displaystyle\\int_{2}^{4}(x^3 - 5x^2 + 2x + 8)\\,dx\\)",null]},
