  "2024 P1 Q2": {"skill":"A recurrence relation: the next term, the condition for a limit, the limit.","method":"(a) 1 mark, 3 marks","moves":["(a) Substitute \\(u_1 = 20\\) into the recurrence relation.","(b)(i) A limit exists when the multiplier is strictly between \\(-1\\) and \\(1\\): say what the multiplier is and that it is.","(b)(ii) At the limit, \\(L = \\frac{1}{5}L + 12\\). Solve for \\(L\\)."],"marks":[1,1,2],"shows":[null,"a limit exists as \\(-1 < \\dfrac{1}{5} < 1\\)","\\(\\dfrac{12}{1 - \\frac{1}{5}}\\) or \\(L = \\dfrac{1}{5}L + 12\\)"]},
  "2024 P1 Q3": {"skill":"Chain rule on a power of a bracket.","method":"2 marks","moves":["Bring the power \\(7\\) down in front and lower the power by \\(1\\), leaving the bracket as it is.","Multiply by the derivative of the bracket, \\(5x^2 + 3\\)."],"marks":[1,1],"shows":["\\(7(5x^2 + 3)^6 \\ldots\\)",null]},
