  "2025 P1 Q8": {"skill":"Finding the base of a logarithm.","method":"3 marks","moves":["Get the logs together on one side: \\(\\log_a 75 - \\log_a 3 = 2\\), then combine them.","Write it without logs: \\(\\frac{75}{3} = a^2\\).","Solve for \\(a\\), remembering \\(a > 0\\)."],"marks":[1,1,1],"shows":["\\(\\log_a \\dfrac{75}{3} = 2\\)","\\(\\dfrac{75}{3} = a^2\\)",null]},
  "2025 P1 Q9": {"skill":"Where a line meets a circle.","method":"4 marks","moves":["Substitute \\(y = x + 1\\) into the circle's equation.","Expand and tidy into a quadratic equal to \\(0\\).","Solve for \\(x\\), then use the line to find each \\(y\\)."],"marks":[1,1,2],"shows":["\\(x^2 + (x + 1)^2 - 2x + 6(x + 1) - 15 (= 0)\\)","\\(2x^2 + 6x - 8 = 0\\)","\\(-4,\\ 1\\)"]},
  "2025 P2 Q1": {"skill":"An altitude, a median, and where they meet.","method":"(a) 3 marks, (b) 3 marks, (c) 2 marks","moves":["(a) The altitude through \\(B\\) is perpendicular to \\(AC\\): find the gradient of \\(AC\\), then the perpendicular gradient.","(a) Use that gradient and point \\(B\\) in \\(y - b = m(x - a)\\).","(b) The median through \\(A\\) goes to the midpoint of \\(BC\\): find that midpoint, then the gradient from \\(A\\).","(b) Write the equation of the median through \\(A\\).","(c) Solve the two equations simultaneously."],"marks":[2,1,2,1,2],"shows":["\\(-\\dfrac{1}{3}\\) or \\(-\\dfrac{10}{30}\\)",null,"\\((15, -2)\\)",null,null]},
  "2025 P2 Q10": {"skill":"Optimising a perimeter.","method":"(a) 3 marks, (b) 6 marks","moves":["(a) Write the perimeter in \\(x\\) and \\(y\\), and write the area (rectangle plus triangle) equal to \\(150\\).","(a) Rearrange the area for \\(y\\), substitute into \\(P\\) and simplify.","(b) Write \\(P\\) with a negative power of \\(x\\), ready to differentiate.","(b) Differentiate and set the derivative equal to \\(0\\).","(b) Solve for \\(x\\).","(b) Show it is a minimum, with a nature table or the second derivative, and substitute to find \\(P\\)."],"marks":[2,1,1,2,1,2],"shows":["\\(P = 12x + 2y\\)","\\(P = 12x + 2\\left(\\dfrac{150 - 6x^2}{5x}\\right)\\) leading to \\(P = 9.6x + \\dfrac{60}{x}\\)","\\(9.6x + 60x^{-1}\\)","\\(9.6 - 60x^{-2}\\)","\\(2.5\\) or \\(\\dfrac{5}{2}\\)","table of signs for a derivative \\(\\therefore\\) minimum, or \\(P''(x) = 120x^{-3}\\) and \\(P''(2.5) = 7.68\\ldots > 0 \\therefore\\) minimum"]},
  "2025 P2 Q11": {"skill":"A trig equation with a double angle, solved by factorising.","method":"4 marks","moves":["Replace \\(\\sin 2x\\) with \\(2\\sin x\\cos x\\).","Take out the common factor \\(\\cos x\\).","Set each factor to \\(0\\) and find every angle in \\(0 \\le x < 360\\)."],"marks":[1,1,2],"shows":["\\(3(2\\sin x^\\circ\\cos x^\\circ) + 4\\cos x^\\circ (= 0)\\)","\\(2\\cos x^\\circ(3\\sin x^\\circ + 2) = 0\\)","\\(\\cos x^\\circ = 0\\), \\(\\sin x^\\circ = -\\dfrac{2}{3}\\)"]},
  "2025 P2 Q12": {"skill":"A composite function, then the chain rule.","method":"(a) 2 marks, (b) 2 marks","moves":["(a) \\(f(g(x))\\) means put \\(g(x) = 1 - x^3\\) into \\(f\\) wherever there is an \\(x\\).","(b) Use the chain rule: bring the power down, lower it by \\(1\\), and multiply by the derivative of the bracket."],"marks":[2,2],"shows":["\\(f(1 - x^3)\\) or \\((g(x))^5 + 3\\)","\\(5(1 - x^3)^4 \\ldots\\)"]},
  "2025 P2 Q13": {"skill":"Exponential decay, solved with logs.","method":"(a) 1 mark, (b) 4 marks","moves":["(a) Initially \\(t = 0\\).","(b) Substitute \\(M = 120\\) and get \\(e^{-0.0054t}\\) on its own.","(b) Take natural logs of both sides and solve for \\(t\\)."],"marks":[1,2,2],"shows":[null,"\\(120 = 150e^{-0.0054t}\\)","\\(\\log_e\\left(\\dfrac{120}{150}\\right) = -0.0054t\\)"]},
  "2025 P2 Q14": {"skill":"Two circles, then a third touching both.","method":"(a) 2 marks, (b) 2 marks, (c) 3 marks","moves":["(a) Read the centre and radius straight from the equation.","(b) Use \\((-g, -f)\\) and \\(r = \\sqrt{g^2 + f^2 - c}\\).","(c) Find the distance between the two centres, and use the diagram to work out the radius of \\(C_3\\).","(c) Find \\(C_3\\)'s centre on the line between the centres, and write its equation."],"marks":[2,2,2,1],"shows":[null,null,"\\(15\\)",null]},
  "2025 P2 Q2": {"skill":"Completing the square with a leading coefficient.","method":"3 marks","moves":["Take out \\(2\\) as a common factor of the \\(x\\) terms only: \\(2(x^2 + 8x) + 5\\).","Complete the square inside: halve \\(8\\) to get \\((x + 4)^2\\), then take away \\(16\\) inside.","Multiply the \\(-16\\) back out by \\(2\\) and collect it with the \\(5\\)."],"marks":[1,1,1],"shows":["\\(2(x^2 + 8x \\ldots\\)","\\(2(x + 4)^2 \\ldots\\)",null]},
